      "countable_problem_unit": true,
      "root_admission_required": true,
      "source_boundary_note": "The complete original Weyl evolution Theorem 4.1 and full author proof are retained for a uniformly bounded C1 Hermitian N-wave solution on the specified semi-strip. Exact fundamental-solution factorization, normalized triangular Weyl/finite-interval graph definitions and recovery are included as author-cited established background. The new positivity-based backward contraction, spatially uniform short-time property-J perturbation, graph limit, denominator invertibility, time-interval iteration and analytic continuation are supplied in full. The explicit uniform commutator/gap threshold and positive diagonal D-hat are retained; D-hat need not be ordered. No N-wave existence/full-rho uniqueness, ordered-D-hat initial-value theorem or dNLS quasi-analytic claim is selected.",
